$ Milestone 7, §5.3/§7/§14: `path.*` -- pure string manipulation, no
$ filesystem access. Deliberately narrow dotted-call syntax (path.join
$ etc.), NOT general member access -- see docs/architecture.md and
$ codegen.cpp's genCall.

bring path

show(path.join("src", "main.fly"))
show(path.join("a", "b", "c"))
show(path.join("/abs", "rel"))
show(path.join("first", "/second"))

show(path.basename("src/main.fly"))
show(path.dirname("src/main.fly"))
show(path.extension("main.fly"))
show(path.extension("README"))
show(path.stem("main.fly"))

sep = path.separator()
show(count(sep))
